---
title: How a document gets masked — language choice and the OCR fallback
---
flowchart TB
    %% Three questions this answers:
    %%   1. Where do Dutch, French and English pseudonyms come from?
    %%   2. Which model reads the document, now that Berts has one per language?
    %%   3. When does OCR run, and when does it not?
    %% Everything between them (reading order, box drawing) is left out on
    %% purpose — see the micro architecture_*.mmd files for that.

    Start(["A file arrives<br/>PDF, plain text, CSV or JSON"]) --> IsPdf{"Is it a PDF?"}
    IsPdf -->|"no"| PlainText["Read the text straight from the file"]
    IsPdf -->|"yes"| Pages

    subgraph Pages["Reading a PDF — each page decided on its own"]
        direction TB
        HasChars{"Does this page have<br/>any real characters in it?<br/>(spaces alone don't count)"}

        HasChars -->|"yes — it has real text"| UseLayer["Use the page's own text"]
        UseLayer --> AlsoImage{"Does it also carry<br/>a picture?"}
        AlsoImage -->|"yes"| Refuse["Refuse the whole document.<br/>Words inside a picture can't be<br/>searched, and half-masked is worse<br/>than not masked."]
        AlsoImage -->|"no"| PageDone(["Page read"])

        HasChars -->|"no — the page is a picture of text"| Ocr["OCR FALLBACK<br/>read the page with PP-OCRv6"]
        Ocr --> Broke{"Did the OCR engine<br/>itself fail?"}
        Broke -->|"yes"| Fault["Server error (500).<br/>Our fault, not the file's —<br/>so the caller can retry."]
        Broke -->|"no"| ReadOk{"Did OCR come back<br/>with any words?"}
        ReadOk -->|"no"| Refuse
        ReadOk -->|"yes"| WriteBack["Put the words back into the PDF<br/>as an invisible text layer, so the rest<br/>of the pipeline treats it like a normal PDF"]
        WriteBack --> PageDone
    end

    OcrOff["If OCR is switched off (PDF_OCR=off)<br/>the fallback branch doesn't exist:<br/>any picture refuses the document."]
    OcrOff -.-> Ocr

    PlainText --> Lang
    PageDone --> Lang

    subgraph Lang["Which language is this document in?"]
        direction TB
        Override{"Did the caller send<br/>X-Document-Locale?"}
        UseGiven(["Use the locale they asked for,<br/>once it is checked<br/>against the known list"])
        Sample["Look at the first 2000 characters<br/>of the whole document"]
        Enough{"At least 40 letters<br/>to judge by?"}
        Score["Score it as Dutch, French or English<br/>(lingua, pinned version)"]
        Sure{"Is the winner at least<br/>70% sure?"}
        Which{"Which one won?"}
        NL(["Dutch → nl_BE"])
        FR(["French → fr_FR"])
        EN(["English → en"])
        Fallback(["Too little to judge<br/>→ fall back to nl_BE"])

        Override -->|"yes"| UseGiven
        Override -->|"no"| Sample
        Sample --> Enough
        Enough -->|"no"| Fallback
        Enough -->|"yes"| Score --> Sure
        Sure -->|"no"| Fallback
        Sure -->|"yes"| Which
        Which -->|"Dutch"| NL
        Which -->|"French"| FR
        Which -->|"English"| EN
    end

    OneVerdict["One verdict for the whole document, decided once, before<br/>anything reads it. It now settles two things that used to be<br/>settled separately: which model reads the document, and<br/>which language the pseudonyms are written in. A page is<br/>never judged on its own — a short page carries no language<br/>signal, and a document that switched model halfway would<br/>mask its second half by different rules than its first."]
    OneVerdict -.-> Lang

    NL --> Find
    FR --> Find
    EN --> Find
    UseGiven --> Find
    Fallback --> Find

    subgraph Find["Finding the values to mask"]
        direction TB
        Routing{"Is per-language routing on?<br/>BERTS_LANGUAGE_ROUTING"}
        Rollback["The way back. Off sends every document to the<br/>Dutch model — what this service did before the<br/>other two existed. A checkpoint that masks badly<br/>is backed out by restarting one service, without<br/>waiting for a release to remove it."]
        Pick{"Which language<br/>did we settle on?"}
        MNL["Dutch model<br/>MedRoBERTa int8"]
        MEN["English model<br/>BERT i2b2 int8"]
        MFR["French model<br/>CamemBERT-bio int8"]
        Loaded["Only the language actually seen is loaded,<br/>and an idle one is dropped again after<br/>MODEL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS — three<br/>checkpoints on disk, rarely three in memory."]
        Model(["The model's guesses<br/>NAME · DATE · ADDRESS · AGE · PHONE · ORGANIZATION"])
        Rules["The rules (regex) read the text"]
        Shared["Same in every language:<br/>INSZ · RIZIV · BTW · IBAN · email · URL<br/>— a checksum does not change with the wording"]
        Words["Language-bound word lists only:<br/>nl 'januari' · 'op' · 'jaar'<br/>fr 'janvier' · 'le' · 'ans'<br/>en 'january' · 'on' · 'years old'"]
        Owned{"Is this a value with a checksum<br/>or a fixed shape?<br/>NIR, RPPS, RIZIV, INSZ, BTW, email, URL,<br/>SSN, NPI, NHS number, GMC"}
        Dropped["Drop the model's guess — the rule<br/>already gives a certain answer"]
        Keep["Keep it"]
        Merged(["One list, overlaps joined"])

        Routing -->|"off"| MNL
        Routing -->|"on"| Pick
        Rollback -.-> Routing
        Pick -->|"nl_BE"| MNL
        Pick -->|"en"| MEN
        Pick -->|"fr_FR"| MFR
        MNL --> Model
        MEN --> Model
        MFR --> Model
        Loaded -.-> Model
        Model --> Owned
        Owned -->|"yes"| Dropped
        Owned -->|"no"| Keep
        Routing --> Rules
        Shared -.-> Rules
        Words -.-> Rules
        Rules --> Keep
        Keep --> Merged
    end

    ThreeModels["All three read the same six kinds of value and were<br/>quantized the same way, so nothing downstream has to know<br/>which one ran. The masked file still says: X-Model-Name<br/>and the model= folder it is written to name the checkpoint."]
    ThreeModels -.-> Find

    NL --> Replace
    FR --> Replace
    EN --> Replace
    UseGiven --> Replace
    Fallback --> Replace
    Merged --> Replace

    Replace["Swap each value for a pseudonym in that language.<br/>The same value always becomes the same pseudonym,<br/>so masking the same file twice gives the same result."]

    LocaleNote["The locale decides the name and address style, the<br/>month names, the gender words, the ending on a masked<br/>web address, and which list of organisation names to<br/>draw from. English carries a medical list only — a<br/>request for the general list falls back to Faker."]
    LocaleNote -.-> Replace

    DateNote["A numeric date is read day-first; if that can't make a<br/>real date, month-first is tried, so 02-17-2026 keeps<br/>its shape whichever way the writer meant it. A written<br/>date is read either way round too — 17 February 2026<br/>and February 17, 2026 both come back in their own shape."]
    DateNote -.-> Replace

    Replace --> Origin{"Where did this value<br/>come from?"}
    Origin -->|"the page's own text"| CleanText["Delete the text.<br/>Leave pictures untouched."]
    Origin -->|"OCR"| CleanBoth["Delete the text <b>and</b> erase the pixels.<br/>Covering them would leave the original<br/>recoverable with any PDF tool."]

    CleanText --> Draw
    CleanBoth --> Draw
    Draw["Draw the pseudonym — or a labelled box —<br/>back in the same spot"]
    Draw --> Out(["Masked file out, same type it came in"])

    classDef stop fill:#fde2e2,stroke:#c23b3b,color:#5a1414
    classDef ocr fill:#e4efff,stroke:#3b6cc2,color:#12305e
    classDef pick fill:#e6f6ea,stroke:#3b9a55,color:#12401f
    classDef model fill:#efe6fb,stroke:#7a4bc2,color:#2f1257
    classDef note fill:#fdf6e3,stroke:#c9a227,color:#5a4708,font-style:italic

    class Refuse,Fault stop
    class Ocr,WriteBack,CleanBoth ocr
    class NL,FR,EN,UseGiven,Fallback,Out pick
    class MNL,MEN,MFR,Model model
    class OcrOff,LocaleNote,DateNote,OneVerdict,ThreeModels,Shared,Words,Loaded,Rollback note
